      "title": "Man found dead on Flinders Island believed to have been shot by officer, police say",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/22/man-found-dead-on-flinders-island-linked-to-shooting-of-police-officer-tasmanian-authorities-say",
      "description": "<p>The sergeant, who was shot, fired his weapon a number of times after alleged ‘targeted’ attack outside island’s police station</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A police officer who was shot outside a remote Tasmanian police station is alleged to have shot and killed his attacker in response to what authorities believe was a “targeted” incident.</p><p>Tasmania police deputy commissioner, Jonathan Higgins, said the sergeant had just come off shift at Whitemark police station on Flinders Island, which is north-east of the Tasmanian mainland. He had parked and gotten out of his police vehicle when he was shot at about 9.45pm on Saturday, Higgins told reporters on Sunday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/22/man-found-dead-on-flinders-island-linked-to-shooting-of-police-officer-tasmanian-authorities-say\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-22T02:44:01"
    },
    {
      "title": "Fred Nile, former NSW politician and figurehead of the rightwing Christian Democratic party, dies aged 92",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/22/fred-nile-former-nsw-politician-and-figurehead-of-the-rightwing-christian-democratic-party-dies-aged-92",
      "description": "<p>Controversial figure frequently took positions against drug use, abortion and homosexuality, but in later years supported legislation expunging homosexual convictions</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The former New South Wales MP and longstanding figurehead of the rightwing Christian Democratic party, the Rev Fred Nile, has died aged 92.</p><p>Nile was a member of the NSW legislative council for more than 40 years. He first entered the state’s upper house in 1981 and retired after unsuccessfully contesting the 2023 election.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/22/fred-nile-former-nsw-politician-and-figurehead-of-the-rightwing-christian-democratic-party-dies-aged-92\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-22T00:26:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Six, seven, maybe more preventable deaths’: Queensland’s LNP faces reckoning over broken health system",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/22/queensland-health-ambulance-deaths-lnp-labor-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>A government in office for more than two years is finally forced to take responsibility and seemingly no longer able to blame its Labor predecessors</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>At the beginning of another Queensland parliamentary sitting week, anonymous sources were out in force, this time background briefing against the state’s Labor leader, Steven Miles.</p><p>It is no great revelation to observers of Queensland politics that Miles, still seemingly bruised from his election loss two years ago, has struggled to find his feet as opposition leader. Many wondered why he wanted to stay on after the party’s drubbing in 2024. Some of Labor’s factional whisperers were telling anyone who would listen that the former premier’s leadership would come to an end in the weeks before Christmas.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/22/queensland-health-ambulance-deaths-lnp-labor-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-21T19:00:08"
    }
